    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>1. COURSE GRADING ELEMENTS：</div>\n\n<div>(1) Literature Review (Critical Analysis) (Midterm presentation) ( Due date: 2024/11/25) - Paper Report 20%</div>\n\n<div>(2) Final Project (Thesis Proposal)(Final presentation) (2024/12/30; 2025/1/6) - Oral Presentation + Paper Report 40%</div>\n\n<div>(3) Midterm examination 25% ( Date: 2024/11/4)</div>\n\n<div>(4) Attendance, Participation and Homework of Information Literacy 15%</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>2. Literature Review (Critical Analysis)： Literature review is an important part of a Master&#39;s thesis. Each student has to submit a written paper prior to the due day, and prepares an oral presentation as well. The guidelines for the written paper will be attached in the &quot;Course Document&quot; section.</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>3. Final Paper： Each student has to submit a written paper prior to the last week of this class. An oral presentation is also required. The objective is to help students compose their thesis proposals ahead of the school schedule. The guidelines for the written paper will be attached in the &quot;Course Document&quot; section.</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>4. Attendance and Participation： Class participation and discussion, including responses to the Discussion Board, are highly recommened. Students who can not attend a certain class should inform the instructor prior to the scheduled class. However, too much absence may affect the grade of this course.</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>1. COURSE GRADING ELEMENTS：</div>\n\n<div>(1) Literature Review (Critical Analysis) (Midterm presentation) ( Due date: 2023/11/27) - Paper Report 20%</div>\n\n<div>(2) Final Project (Thesis Proposal)(Final presentation) (2023/12/25; 2024/1/8) - Oral Presentation + Paper Report 40%</div>\n\n<div>(3) Midterm examination 25% ( Date: 2023/11/6)</div>\n\n<div>(4) Attendance, Participation and Homework of Information Literacy 15%</div>\n",
    "course_pol": "應課前預習指定進度。\n確認小組成員, 分組討論。\n上課參與討論並發表想法。\n遵守授課老師排定日期(期中報告以及期末報告)，準時完成學習成果。\n未參與報告製作或繳交相關指定報告考試的同學，成績不予評分。(除因特殊情況經授課老師同意者不在此限。)",
    "course_pol_en": "1. Literature Review (Critical Analysis)： Literature review is an important part of a Master's thesis. Each student has to submit a written paper prior to the due day, and prepares an oral presentation as well. The guidelines for the written paper will be attached in the \"Course Document\" section.\n \n2. Final Paper： Each student has to submit a written paper prior to the last week of this class. An oral presentation is also required. The objective is to help students compose their thesis proposals ahead of the school schedule. The guidelines for the written paper will be attached in the \"Course Document\" section.\n \n3. Attendance and Participation： Class participation and discussion, including responses to the Discussion Board, are highly recommened. Students who can not attend a certain class should inform the instructor prior to the scheduled class. However, too much absence may affect the grade of this course.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>學生應尊重學術道德，避免未經授權使用他人作品。</div>\n\n<div>禁止任何抄襲、作弊、偽造或違反著作權法...等違反學術倫理之行為。</div>\n\n<div>所有資料來源須清楚說明，相關文獻引用須適當。</div>\n\n<div>如違反學術誠信與倫理之行為，將自行承擔所有法律責任，以及概括承受一切後果。</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>\n<div>Students should respect academic ethics and avoid unauthorized use of the work of others.</div>\n</div>\n\n<div>Any behavior that violates academic ethics such as plagiarism, cheating, forgery, or violation of copyright laws is prohibited.</div>\n\n<div>All sources of information must be clearly stated and relevant literature cited appropriately.</div>\n\n<div>\n<div>If you violate academic integrity and ethics, you will bear all legal responsibilities and bear all consequences.</div>\n</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
